; A one-argument primitive applied to nothing, or passed bare. A
; primitive is lowered in place at every call and has no function
; symbol, so unlike a one-parameter `fn` - whose bare name is a thunk -
; it has no value to take. Both shapes checked OK and emitted
; `%__floatToInt`, a register nothing defines, which llc refused
; (tests/fuzz/primitive-value.axfuzz, found by the seeded fuzzer
; 2026-09-27); thirteen primitives were open to it. Every primitive of
; two or more arguments was AX3013 already, and these are now the same.
;
; `(__argc)` takes NO argument, so the one-element list is its call, and
; it stays legal; so does `useOne`, a one-parameter `fn` passed as a
; value.
(:: apply (-> (-> Int Int) Int Int))
(fn (apply f x)
  (f x))

(:: one (-> Int Int))
(fn (one x)
  x)

(:: appliedToNothing Int)
(fn (appliedToNothing)
  (__floatToInt))

(:: passedBare Int)
(fn (passedBare)
  (apply __atomic_load 8))

(:: useOne Int)
(fn (useOne)
  (apply one 8))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (__argc))
